\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
If a division ring D is generated as an algebra by finitely many elements over its center F and every element of D is algebraic over F, must [D:F] be finite?

\subsection{Short English statement}
If a division ring D is generated as an algebra by finitely many elements over its center F and every element of D is algebraic over F, must [D:F] be finite?

